From: pocket-debs <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 13:06:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] notificationmanager: no unread count from the server models with the watcher source
Description:
 With the watcher source there is no portal notifications model; an expired
 portal notification dereferenced it while counting unread notifications.
Author: masterxq <masterxq@users.noreply.github.com>
Forwarded: no
License: LGPL-2.1-only OR LGPL-3.0-only OR LicenseRef-KDE-Accepted-LGPL (as the patched files)
Last-Update: 2026-11-28
---
diff --git a/libnotificationmanager/notifications.cpp b/libnotificationmanager/notifications.cpp
index f75830770b..92b05d4bb6 100644
--- a/libnotificationmanager/notifications.cpp
+++ b/libnotificationmanager/notifications.cpp
@@ -352,7 +352,8 @@ void Notifications::Private::updateCount()
                 date = idx.data(Notifications::CreatedRole).toDateTime();
             }
 
-            if ((Portal::isPortalNotificationId(Private::notificationId(idx)) && date > portalNotificationsModel->lastRead())
+            // the server models are not there with the watcher source
+            if ((Portal::isPortalNotificationId(Private::notificationId(idx)) && portalNotificationsModel && date > portalNotificationsModel->lastRead())
                 || (notificationsModel && date > notificationsModel->lastRead())) {
                 ++unread;
             }
